WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:02.260
- [Christian] Modern furniture began

00:00:02.260 --> 00:00:05.150
at the Bauhaus 100 years ago.

00:00:05.150 --> 00:00:08.960
There have always been only
a few serious companies

00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:12.390
doing Bauhaus furniture
re-editions or replicas.

00:00:12.390 --> 00:00:14.100
We are doing this for 50 years now.

00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:16.510
It's important for us to tell the story

00:00:16.510 --> 00:00:17.993
how it really was.

00:00:22.970 --> 00:00:24.680
- [Narrator] This is Tecta,

00:00:24.680 --> 00:00:27.220
a factory in Lauenförde, Germany-

00:00:27.220 --> 00:00:28.450
one of the few in the world

00:00:28.450 --> 00:00:30.883
to replicate original Bauhaus furniture.

00:00:31.950 --> 00:00:34.563
And this is one of the
crafters behind it all.

00:00:35.790 --> 00:00:37.027
- My name is Christian Drescher.

00:00:37.027 --> 00:00:39.800
I'm the owner of Tecta.

00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:42.720
We are a family business
fourth generations,

00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:45.930
and I co-work with my
uncle, Axel Bruchhäuser,

00:00:45.930 --> 00:00:47.480
for the last years.

00:00:47.480 --> 00:00:51.610
- With my father and I, we
took over the existing company,

00:00:51.610 --> 00:00:55.890
Tecta, and our dream was to produce

00:00:55.890 --> 00:00:59.780
all the forgotten Bauhaus furnitures.

00:00:59.780 --> 00:01:01.840
- Our aim is to prove everyday

00:01:01.840 --> 00:01:03.730
that these classics still play a role

00:01:03.730 --> 00:01:06.000
in current living situations.

00:01:06.000 --> 00:01:08.530
- The centenarian designs
are known for their minimal

00:01:08.530 --> 00:01:11.470
and practical nature and lack
of adornments and details-

00:01:11.470 --> 00:01:13.970
central features in the Bauhaus school.

00:01:13.970 --> 00:01:16.010
And these men are on an intricate mission

00:01:16.010 --> 00:01:19.630
to make sure that designs
like the 1925 Wassily Chair

00:01:19.630 --> 00:01:23.980
and the 1927 Cantilever
Chair are still sat on today.

00:01:23.980 --> 00:01:28.980
- Drawings and original
documentations are very important.

00:01:29.170 --> 00:01:31.860
So we worked closely, or work closely,

00:01:31.860 --> 00:01:34.290
with the Bauhaus archive
and then, from that on,

00:01:34.290 --> 00:01:38.187
we can realize things; we
have a carpentry workshop

00:01:38.187 --> 00:01:40.170
and a metal workshop, the upholstery,

00:01:40.170 --> 00:01:42.989
put all these together,
together with the designer;

00:01:42.989 --> 00:01:47.130
this makes it possible
to make the furniture.

00:01:47.130 --> 00:01:51.967
It's a big satisfaction if
you see that you have somehow

00:01:51.967 --> 00:01:54.770
prolonged the life-cycle of an old classic

00:01:54.770 --> 00:01:58.040
by doing an interpretation of 2019

00:01:58.040 --> 00:02:00.838
of a Bauhaus piece from 1919.

00:02:00.838 --> 00:02:04.487
And then people say, "Wow,
this is so avantgardistic,

00:02:04.487 --> 00:02:07.890
"this is so contemporary"
though it's 100 years old.

00:02:07.890 --> 00:02:10.050
That makes us very proud

00:02:10.050 --> 00:02:11.600
because they are not simple products.

00:02:11.600 --> 00:02:16.057
They are furniture with a
soul with something more.

00:02:16.057 --> 00:02:18.557
(light music)

